@startuml Geometry_State
title Geometry - State Machine (proposed)

' Source of inspiration:
'   XrayGenerator/src/main.cpp - the sister I2C-slave structure
'   System requirements (operator joystick + button, SAN line on the bus)
'   Geometry/src/main.cpp      - current skeleton (only stubs implemented)
'
' Role: I2C slave (intended I2C_ADDR_SLAVE_2; the skeleton currently uses
'       SLAVE_1, which collides with XrayGenerator and needs fixing).
'       The Geometry positions the C-arm / detector. While idle it is
'       under operator control (joystick or fixed-speed button). During
'       an exam it is mostly passive, EXCEPT for SERIES_WITH_MOTION,
'       where it sweeps along a programmed motion profile and uses the
'       SAN line to fire the X-ray Generator at each sample point.
'
'   SAN contract (open-drain, pulled HIGH by default):
'     - SAN floats HIGH while geometry is stationary or under operator
'       control during Idle.
'     - SAN is driven LOW by Geometry while it is moving during the
'       SERIES_WITH_MOTION exam, which the XrayGenerator samples to fire.
'
'   I2C event handling on the slave side is identical in shape to the
'   XrayGenerator: onReceive() updates {lastResponse, lastPayloadOutgoing},
'   onRequest() returns them and resets lastResponse to NAK.

[*] --> Idle

state Idle {
  [*] --> Stationary

  state Stationary       : motors off\nSAN = HIGH (released)
  state JoystickMove     : speed = f(joystick deflection)\ndrive motors\nSAN = HIGH
  state FixedSpeedMove   : speed = FIXED_SPEED\ndrive motors\nSAN = HIGH

  Stationary     --> JoystickMove   : |joystick| > deadzone
  JoystickMove   --> Stationary     : joystick centered
  Stationary     --> FixedSpeedMove : button pressed
  JoystickMove   --> FixedSpeedMove : button pressed\n(button overrides joystick)
  FixedSpeedMove --> Stationary     : button released

  Idle : on MSG_HEARTBEAT  / lastPayloadOutgoing = posStatus, lastResponse = ACK
  Idle : on MSG_DATA_READY / lastPayloadOutgoing = posStatus, lastResponse = ACK
  Idle : on MSG_STOP       / lastPayloadOutgoing = 0x00,      lastResponse = ACK
  Idle : on MSG_ERROR      / (no-op, future)
  Idle : on unknown msg    / lastResponse = NAK
}

' ---- Dispatch on MSG_START -------------------------------------------------
state "Exam\n(MSG_START)" as Exam {
  [*] --> ChoosePayload

  state ChoosePayload <<choice>>

  state ExamNone        : stop motors\nSAN = HIGH
  state ExamSingleShot  : hold position\nSAN = HIGH\n(no motion needed)
  state ExamSeries      : hold position\nSAN = HIGH\n(no motion needed)

  state SeriesWithMotion {
    [*] --> Sweeping
    state Sweeping       : drive motors along\nprogrammed profile\nSAN = LOW (fires X-ray)
    state BetweenSamples : motors paused briefly\nSAN = HIGH
    Sweeping       --> BetweenSamples : sample point reached
    BetweenSamples --> Sweeping       : next sample due\n[shotCount < N]
    BetweenSamples --> [*]            : shotCount == N\nor end of profile
  }

  state ExamFluoro      : hold position\nSAN = HIGH\n(no motion needed)

  ChoosePayload --> ExamNone          : [EXAM_TYPE_NONE]
  ChoosePayload --> ExamSingleShot    : [EXAM_TYPE_SINGLE_SHOT]
  ChoosePayload --> ExamSeries        : [EXAM_TYPE_SERIES]
  ChoosePayload --> SeriesWithMotion  : [EXAM_TYPE_SERIES_WITH_MOTION]
  ChoosePayload --> ExamFluoro        : [EXAM_TYPE_FLUORO]

  ExamNone         --> [*]
  ExamSingleShot   --> [*] : MSG_STOP received\nor exam end
  ExamSeries       --> [*] : MSG_STOP received\nor exam end
  ExamFluoro       --> [*] : MSG_STOP received\nor exam end
}

Idle --> Exam : MSG_START\n/ lastResponse = ACK,\n  branch on lastPayloadIncoming\n  freeze operator input
Exam --> Idle : run-to-completion\n/ motors off, SAN = HIGH,\n  resume operator input

' ---- I2C response side (read path) ----
state ResponseRead : onRequest() writes\n{lastResponse, lastPayloadOutgoing}\nthen lastResponse = NAK

Idle --> ResponseRead : onRequest()
Exam --> ResponseRead : onRequest()\n(busy during exam -> NAK)
ResponseRead --> Idle : return

note right of Exam
  Only SERIES_WITH_MOTION actually moves
  during the exam. It is the source of the
  SAN LOW pulses that the XrayGenerator
  samples (see XrayGenerator's
  ExposeSeriesMotion state: "on SAN==LOW
  toggle PORTB").

  The other exam types ack and hold
  position because the X-ray Generator
  drives its own SAN-pin loop directly
  from the operator's Xray button.
end note

note left of Idle
  Operator input is only honored while
  Idle. Entering the Exam composite
  freezes the joystick / button inputs
  so a stray operator press cannot
  perturb a programmed sweep.
end note

@enduml
